				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jpadilly" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2261765); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2261765&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607546998" alt="JPadilly" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2261765)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jpadilly" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2261765); return false;" >JPadilly</a></span> <span class="odate time_1441648844 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Sep 2015 18:00</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2371361">
									

<p>The only thing that redeemed it for me was the test logs. As an SCP, it was pretty predictable. Without the test logs, it didn't even seem threatening or terrible past 'unexplained technology.' I think, as augmentedspartan said, that the question of what makes it possible is the only thing that's really intriguing. And maybe add something past Ultra-Realism mode that IS unpredictable, if not replacing it.</p>
<p>The AI is interesting, but it's unclear what it's rules of sentients are. First it says what the D-Class can call it, then it acts like a busted machine, and it never seems to address the D-Class as though it recognizes him. Maybe it's just me, but the specifics get confusing.</p>
<p>I'll also agree with everyone else, though; The test log is fantastic.</p>

